   "body": "# Obama O's and Cap'n McCain's: The Cereal That Saved Airbnb\n\n**One-line hook:** Broke and in debt, the Airbnb founders sold novelty cereal during the 2008 election, and it got them into Y Combinator.\n\n## The Story\nBy 2008 the young Airbnb was barely alive. Few people were booking, investors kept passing, and the founders had piled up **credit card debt**. With the U.S. presidential election heating up, Brian Chesky and Joe Gebbia had an odd idea: sell **limited-edition cereal boxes** themed on the candidates, **\"Obama O's\"** and **\"Cap'n McCain's.\"**\n\nThey designed the boxes themselves, bought cheap cereal, and assembled the boxes by hand. The stunt got press coverage, and they sold enough at a premium price to pay off a big chunk of their debt and keep going.\n\nThe cereal mattered most when they interviewed at **Y Combinator**. Paul Graham wasn't impressed by the Airbnb idea itself, but the cereal story showed him the founders were **resourceful and very hard to kill**. He accepted them, reportedly saying something to the effect that if they could get people to pay that much for cereal, they could probably get people to rent out their homes.\n\n## The Lesson\n**Investors and bosses often bet on the people more than the idea.** A creative way of surviving can be the best proof of your ability.\n\n## When to Use This\n- You're stuck and running out of time or money\n- You need to show grit in an interview or pitch\n- Your main project is stalled and you need a creative side move\n- You're judging which team or person to back\n\n## Try This\n- In your next interview or pitch, tell one specific story of how you got out of a tight spot.\n- When stuck, brainstorm ten weird ways to raise money, attention, or time, and try the least risky one.\n\n## Related\n- [[Shoe Dog]]: Phil Knight's constant cash crises\n- [[Originals]]: unusual moves by creative founders\n- [[The Obstacle Is the Way]]: turning obstacles into fuel\n\n## Aha Prompt\n*\"What scrappy move would prove I'm too stubborn to quit?\"*"
