   "verified": false,
   "body": "# Demosthenes Trains His Voice with Pebbles\n\n**One-line hook:** A sickly boy with a speech problem became the greatest speaker of ancient Athens.\n\n## The Story\n**Demosthenes** was born weak and sickly in ancient Athens, with a **speech impediment**. His father died when he was young, and the guardians who were supposed to protect his inheritance **stole it** instead.\n\nHe decided to become a great speaker so he could fight back in court. Holiday describes his famous training: he spoke with **pebbles in his mouth** to improve his diction, practiced speeches while running or out of breath, and spoke over the **roar of the waves** at the sea so his voice would be strong. He built an underground study and, to force himself to stay inside and practice, **shaved half his head** so he would be too embarrassed to go out.\n\nEventually he took his guardians to court and won. He went on to become one of the most famous orators in history. Holiday's point: the very weakness that held him back became the thing he **mastered**.\n\n## The Lesson\nYour weakness can become your strength if you **train directly against it**. Obstacles make the practice harder, and therefore make you better.\n\n## When to Use This\n- You're bad at a skill your career needs (speaking, writing, coding)\n- You feel behind because of a weak start\n- You're tempted to avoid the thing you struggle with\n- You need to commit to a hard practice plan\n\n## Try This\n- Pick your biggest weakness and design a daily drill that targets it directly.\n- Remove an escape route that lets you skip practice.\n\n## Related\n- [[Outliers]]: the hours behind mastery\n- [[Hidden Potential]]: growth from weakness\n- [[David and Goliath]]: how disadvantages can become advantages\n\n## Aha Prompt\n*\"What weakness could I turn into my edge if I practiced it daily?\"*"
