   "body": "# The Man Who Didn't Want to Be in Anand\n\n**One-line hook:** The \"Milkman of India\" arrived in Anand bored, unhappy and counting the days until he could leave.\n\n## The Story\nVerghese Kurien had trained as an engineer and studied abroad on a government scholarship. In return, he was **bound to serve** the government. He was posted to a government creamery in **Anand**, a small town in Gujarat. He did not want to be there, did not care much about dairying, and planned to leave as soon as his bond was done.\n\nNearby, a small farmers' cooperative, led by **Tribhuvandas Patel**, was struggling with old equipment. Kurien began helping them fix machines in his spare time. Tribhuvandas asked him to stay and help the cooperative. Kurien agreed to stay for a while. That \"while\" became the rest of his career. The cooperative grew into **Amul**, and Kurien helped bring the model to the whole country.\n\nWhat changed was not the place but his **reason for being there**. Working for farmers who owned their own business gave the job meaning that the government post never had.\n\n## The Lesson\nA job you dislike can turn into your life's work when you **find a purpose and people worth serving** inside it. Meaning often comes from commitment, not before it.\n\n## When to Use This\n- You feel stuck in a role you didn't choose\n- You're waiting out a job until \"the real thing\" starts\n- Deciding whether to say yes to a small side request\n- Feeling behind peers who seem to have better paths\n\n## Try This\n- Look for one person or group near you whose problem you could help solve this month.\n- Say yes to a small, low-risk commitment and see whether it gives you energy.\n\n## Related\n- [[Start with Why]]: purpose turns work into a mission\n- [[Range]]: careers found by experimenting, not early planning\n- [[Hidden Potential]]: growth comes from what you do, not where you start\n\n## Aha Prompt\n*\"What small problem near me could become worth staying for?\"*"
