   "verified": false,
   "body": "# The Maruti 800 and the Car India Was Waiting For\n\n**One-line hook:** India had waited decades for a modern, affordable car, and when it came, demand was far bigger than supply.\n\n## The Story\nBefore Maruti, Indian buyers had only a few old car models to choose from. They were costly, outdated, and often had long waiting lists. Many people thought ordinary Indian families could not afford a car, so there was no market for one.\n\nMaruti bet the other way. It launched the **Maruti 800**, a small, fuel-efficient, modern car priced for the middle class. In December 1983, Prime Minister **Indira Gandhi** handed over the keys of the first car to a buyer, **Harpal Singh**. Bookings were so large that cars were allotted through a **draw**, because demand far exceeded production.\n\nBhargava shows that the \"no market\" belief was wrong. There was **hidden demand** that old products had never served. Once a good product came at the right price, families who had never thought about a car became buyers. Maruti then grew production and a supplier network to match the demand it had found.\n\n## The Lesson\n\"There's no market\" often means **\"nobody has offered the right product at the right price yet.\"** Weak demand for bad options says little about demand for a good one.\n\n## When to Use This\n- Someone says customers \"won't pay\" for something new\n- An industry has few choices and long waits\n- Deciding whether to price for the mass market\n- Launching a product into a market that looks small\n\n## Try This\n- Ask: \"Is demand low, or are current options just poor?\" Look for long waits, complaints and workarounds.\n- Design for the price your target customer can pay, then work backward to the product.\n\n## Related\n- [[Zero to One]]: creating a new market instead of fighting in an old one\n- [[Blue Ocean Strategy]]: unlocking non-customers\n- [[The Everything Store]]: obsessing over price and customer value\n\n## Aha Prompt\n*\"Who isn't buying today only because nobody has made the right thing for them?\"*"
