   "body": "# The NCX-10: An Hour Lost at the Bottleneck Is an Hour Lost for Everyone\n\n**One-line hook:** The plant's most important machine was sitting idle at lunch, and nobody thought that mattered.\n\n## The Story\nOnce Alex Rogo's team finds their bottlenecks, an expensive **NCX-10** machine and the **heat-treat** department, Jonah visits and walks the floor with them. They discover the NCX-10 is **idle during lunch breaks and shift changes**. Some parts reach it that will later be **scrapped for defects**, so bottleneck time is spent on bad parts. Heat-treat is processing parts that aren't needed for any current order.\n\nJonah's rule: **an hour lost at a bottleneck is an hour lost for the whole system**. An hour saved at a non-bottleneck is a mirage. The team makes changes: they keep the bottleneck running through breaks, move **quality checks in front of** the bottleneck so it only works on good parts, mark bottleneck parts so they get **priority**, and bring back an older machine (the Zmegma) to take some load off the NCX-10. Throughput goes up without major new spending.\n\nThese steps become Goldratt's way of improving: **identify** the constraint, **exploit** it, **subordinate** everything else to it, **elevate** it, and then **repeat** when the constraint moves.\n\n## The Lesson\n**Protect and fully use your constraint before spending money on more capacity.** Most bottlenecks waste a lot of their time on things that don't matter.\n\n## When to Use This\n- Your scarcest expert spends time on admin or low-value work\n- You're about to buy or hire capacity to fix a slow process\n- Rework is landing on your busiest person or step\n- The bottleneck sits idle while everyone else is busy\n\n## Try This\n- Watch your bottleneck for a day and log every minute it's idle or doing work that will be thrown away.\n- Put a quality check right before the bottleneck so it only handles good inputs.\n\n## Related\n- [[The Toyota Way]]: building quality in at each step\n- [[The 80/20 Principle]]: focusing on the few things that matter most\n- [[Extreme Ownership]]: \"prioritize and execute\"\n\n## Aha Prompt\n*\"What is my bottleneck wasting time on right now?\"*"
