   "verified": false,
   "body": "# The Plateau Trap: Why People Quit Right Before It Works\n\n**One-line hook:** The moment you feel like quitting is often the moment progress is happening below the surface.\n\n## The Story\n*Note: this page summarizes one of the book's core principles rather than a specific anecdote from it.*\n\nA theme running through The 1% Rule is the clash between **instant gratification and long-term mastery**. We live surrounded by quick hits, such as fast results, quick wins and constant feedback, so we expect progress to feel steady and visible. Real skill-building doesn't work that way. It has **long flat stretches** where effort goes in and nothing seems to come out.\n\nBaker's argument is that these **plateaus are part of the process, not a sign of failure**. Most people read the plateau as proof they've hit their limit or chosen the wrong path, and they switch to something new, starting over at zero. People who reach mastery keep doing the daily work through the boring middle. They measure themselves by **whether they showed up**, not by whether they saw results that day.\n\nThe practical shift is from chasing **outcomes** to committing to **inputs**. You can't control when the breakthrough comes. You can control whether you did today's 1%.\n\n## The Lesson\nPlateaus are normal. **Judge yourself by consistency of effort, not speed of results**, and don't quit in the flat part of the curve.\n\n## When to Use This\n- You've been working on something for months and feel stuck\n- You're tempted to jump to a new method, job or goal because progress stalled\n- A team initiative looks like it isn't working yet\n- You're coaching someone who wants fast results\n\n## Try This\n- Swap your outcome goal for an input goal: \"Write 300 words a day\" instead of \"finish the book.\"\n- Before quitting anything, write down how long you've *really* been consistent. Has it been long enough to judge?\n\n## Related\n- [[The Obstacle Is the Way]]: persistence and focusing on what you control\n- [[Hidden Potential]]: getting unstuck when progress stalls\n- [[Shoe Dog]]: years of grinding before Nike took off\n\n## Aha Prompt\n*\"Am I actually failing, or am I just in the flat part of the curve?\"*"
