   "verified": false,
   "body": "# The Engineer Who Drove Across North America to Redesign a Minivan\n\n**One-line hook:** Toyota's chief engineer didn't study market reports about American families; he drove the roads they drive.\n\n## The Story\nWhen Toyota was redesigning the **Sienna** minivan for North America, the chief engineer, **Yuji Yokoya**, had never lived there. Instead of relying on reports, he practiced **genchi genbutsu**: \"go and see for yourself.\" He **drove a Sienna through every U.S. state, every Canadian province, and Mexico**.\n\nAlong the way he noticed things no survey would have told him. Roads and **crosswinds** in some regions called for better handling and stability. In some places the streets were narrow, so the van needed a **tighter turning radius**. Most important, he saw how American families actually used minivans: kids and long trips, with lots of eating and drinking in the car. That led to more **cup holders** and room inside. He realized that in a minivan, the children in the back seats matter as much as the driver.\n\nThe redesigned Sienna was a big improvement, because it was designed around how people really lived.\n\n## The Lesson\n**You can't understand a problem from a desk.** Go to where the work or the customer actually is and see it with your own eyes.\n\n## When to Use This\n- You're designing a product for users you've never met\n- You're managing a team or market in a different country\n- Reports say one thing but results say another\n- You're about to make a decision based only on a summary\n\n## Try This\n- Before your next big decision, spend time where the problem happens: shadow a user, sit with the front line, walk the process.\n- Write down three things you saw that weren't in any report.\n\n## Related\n- [[The Airbnb Story]]: the founders flew to New York to meet hosts and photograph their homes\n- [[The Everything Store]]: Bezos's focus on the customer\n- [[Talking to Strangers]]: why our guesses about other people are often wrong\n\n## Aha Prompt\n*\"Have I actually gone and seen this problem, or only read about it?\"*"
